    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **53 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership level 4 rule in `MembershipLevels.of()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevels.java`).\n\n**The change:**\n- Added a fourth factor: `+1` when tenure exceeds 365 days, and raised the cap from 3 to 4.\n- Tenure is computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())`, with a null registration date treated as 0 days.\n\n**Why a new owner never exceeds level 3:** `BuildOwner` sets a new owner's `registrationDate` to today, so its tenure is 0 \u2014 never `> 365`. The maximum a new owner can score is `1 (base) + 1 (email) + 1 (namesakeCount == 0) = 3`. Household size is not a level factor (confirmed by the pre-existing Cp23 test, where a 3-member household with no email lands at level 2), so the \"3-member household\" case in the spec still yields level 3, not 4. Level 4 only becomes reachable once an owner accrues more than a year of tenure.\n\nBoth the new `Cp39Tests` (new owner capped at level 3) and all pre-existing membership tests (Cp13/14/15/23/24) remain green.",
